  },
  "gotchas": [
    {
      "severity": "warn",
      "text": "The driver reported thermal/hardware slowdown during the run — the numbers are throttled."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "link": "https://github.com/0xBakeer/deepseek-v4-flash-spark",
      "text": "The served stack is published as a recipe: https://github.com/0xBakeer/deepseek-v4-flash-spark v0.1.0 pins exllamav3-anemone c6d2e3e plus an aarch64 patch, TabbyAPI 4a4f9f4 plus a unified-memory patch, the chat template, the sampler preset and this exact config, and ships it as the image ghcr.io/0xbakeer/deepseek-v4-flash-spark. These rows were served by the recipe's native install (docs/build-from-source.md) on the DGX Spark rather than the container; engine.build names the recipe tag because the fork sha alone does not describe the served build."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "link": "https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731/blob/main/encoding/encoding_dsv4.py",
      "text": "Thinking is ON in every row with reasoning_effort max, set server-side through template_vars_default (the recipe's config with thinking true and effort max, otherwise identical to its served config); requests sent no chat_template_kwargs. The chat template is the recipe's 1:1 port of DeepSeek's reference encoder, not the pack's reconstructed chat_template.jinja, which ignores the thinking switch. The thinking-off rows on this cell are config 299da4b40264e1ab; template-vars-default is the only argument that differs."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "TabbyAPI only returns a usage block on a non-streaming completion when the request carries stream_options.include_usage; the harness's tokenizer fallback counts prompt tokens but not completions. Every request here sends stream_options {\"include_usage\": true} via the packet's extra_body, so output token counts are the engine's own and include the reasoning tokens."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "DeepSeek-V4's DSA attention keeps a tiny paged fp16 pool (about 2.5 GiB at 384k tokens, 5 GiB for the 768k cache-size here, plus 1.1 GiB for the drafter), so context is not memory-limited on this pack: 393216 per request with a 786432-token pool leaves two full conversations prefix-cached at 106 GB used. cache-quant fp16 is the effective mode either way - k,v bit settings are ignored for DSA layers."
    },
    {
      "severity": "warn",
      "text": "With thinking on, the reasoning tokens count against each eval's fixed max_output_tokens (256-4096 per workload) and its 300 s timeout, and they are not separable from the answer in the completion budget. eval-longgen-integrity-v1 scores 0/36 with every item judged \"empty output\" at 2994 tokens: the 3000-token cap was consumed by reasoning before any content was emitted, so that row measures the budget, not generation integrity. eval-code-v1 lost 4 items to the 300 s timeout and more to cap-truncated answers. Compare capability against the thinking-off rows (config 299da4b40264e1ab) on those two workloads."
    }
  ],
